To determine how long Mike's money will last, we begin by calculating his total earnings:

- Earnings from mowing lawns: $14  
- Earnings from weed eating: $26  

So, the total amount of money Mike has is:

$$
14 + 26 = 40 \text{ dollars}
$$

Next, we consider the rate at which Mike spends his money. The problem states that he spends **$5 per week**. To find out how long the money will last, we divide the total amount by the weekly expenditure:

$$
40 \div 5 = 8 \text{ weeks}
$$

This calculation shows that the money will last Mike exactly 8 weeks, assuming he continues to spend $5 per week without any additional income or savings.

